        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers, or make your own offer. Register now at SherryFitz.ie.\n\nNo. 71 Old Balreask Woods is a well-presented three-bedroom semi-detached home, ideally positioned within this highly regarded and established residential development on the Dublin side of Navan. Having been carefully maintained and well cared for by the current owners, the property offers comfortable and practical accommodation throughout. Also to note within the property is a recently renovated ensuite that adds a modern flavour to the residence. An ideal choice for first-time buyers, young families or those looking to make the most of its excellent location.\n\nOne of the standout features of this property is the spacious rear garden, providing an excellent outdoor space for families, entertaining or simply enjoying the warmer months. The garden also offers plenty of scope for those wishing to further enhance the outdoor space, subject to the necessary planning permissions. To the front, there is off-street parking and the property benefits from the established setting and mature surroundings associated with Old Balreask Woods. \n\nThe location is a major attraction, with the development situated within easy reach of Navan town centre. A wide selection of amenities are close by, including primary and secondary schools, supermarkets, shopping facilities, sporting clubs, recreational amenities and the River Boyne, while the town centre provides an extensive choice of shops, cafés, restaurants and everyday services. \n\nThe surrounding area also offers excellent opportunities for walking and outdoor recreation, with nearby green spaces and riverside walks adding to the appeal of the location.\n\nFor commuters, the property is particularly well positioned, with the M3 motorway interchange only a few minutes' drive away, providing excellent connectivity towards Dublin and beyond. Dublin city can be reached in approximately 4550 minutes outside peak traffic, making this an appealing location for those who commute while still wanting to enjoy the benefits of living in Navan.\n\nOverall, No. 71 Old Balreask Woods represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a well-cared-for family home in a popular and convenient residential setting. With its spacious rear garden, established surroundings, proximity to Navan town and superb access to the M3 motorway, this property is sure to appeal to a wide range of purchasers."
